                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c18061e-8357-3f5f-aa0c-5522de8de9e1",
                                        "entry_id": "b9bcd283-8da9-33bb-81c6-cb5dad100277",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Short and stocky."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96bd7544-c585-4751-a7e9-ebc4d888bd26",
                                                "sense_id": "4c18061e-8357-3f5f-aa0c-5522de8de9e1",
                                                "text": "The study of biotype also led to interesting conclusions: 53 patients were normolineal, 28 longilineal and only 19 brevilineal; actually , some represented an intermediate type , to which White has called attention: athletic, muscular, overweight subjects, whome Sheldon classified as endomorph-mesomorphs, that is brevilineal tending to normolineal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7418146-f60f-45e9-add3-17a0f2802b68",
                                                "sense_id": "4c18061e-8357-3f5f-aa0c-5522de8de9e1",
                                                "text": "The three basic body types marked different fertility types: brevilineal was cast as the most fertile woman at the top of the scale, longuilineal at the bottom, with the normal types in the middle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce6410fa-5260-42c2-b67f-306cab5c5c72",
                                                "sense_id": "4c18061e-8357-3f5f-aa0c-5522de8de9e1",
                                                "text": "This is more prominent in brevilineal individuals, and thus the origin of the left lower lobe (LLL) bronchus is accessible in rigid bronchoscopy only by using small tubes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
